            <ArticleTitle>Neurogastroenterology: Neuronal correlates of placebo in chronic FGIDs.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>460-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nrgastro.2014.118</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Placebo analgesia is increasingly appreciated in many difficult to treat chronic functional gastrointestinal disorders such as IBS. However, investigations of interactions between psychological and biological placebo factors are still in early stages. Now, technologies have been developed that enable neural mechanisms of placebo analgesia to be studied more directly in humans.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
